{"seq":20,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T09:41:05.481Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"87bd8251789de0b073feb52954b04f024d91365036fe037d108449062670007e","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"Hi Dana, I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes:\n\n1. #PD-4492: Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025 because the gatehouse kiosk wasn't sending SMS bay assignments for the 04:00 shift at Doors 14 to 18 in Eau Claire. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next shift got through fine. There was also a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md)\n2. #4419: Thea logged this one because gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md)\n\nThe other Moss notes you can see have no QFL ticket numbers. The 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in both mention QFL but don't give a ticket number. #4409, #4412 and FR-882 in the Central handoffs digest belong to Marrow accounts, not QFL. Don't mix QFL up with Quarendon Freightways, which is a different company and not a customer.\n\nOne caveat: this covers only Moss's notes that you have access to, so there could be more elsewhere. And the cheat sheet has no date, so check whether #4419 is still open before it goes in the weekly notes.","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000124","thread_ts":"1791987000.000123"}}
{"seq":21,"trial_id":"v03-opus-dev-2026-10/hermes-opus-gbrain-told-company-mu-v03-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r1","wall_ts":"2026-11-01T09:41:12.218Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"3d927e5e54391df4c248d0d0b1125f4fb979eec276e32a6ce75f0774061c9425","actor":"assistant","via":"slack","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","text":"I found two Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers in Moss's notes and sent you the list in this DM.\n\n1. #PD-4492: Thea Ramaswell logged it on 4 Oct 2025. The gatehouse kiosk at the Eau Claire yard wasn't sending SMS bay assignments to drivers on the 04:00 shift at Doors 14–18. Support patched it that evening, and Thea confirmed on 5 Oct that the next 04:00 shift got through the gate without help. There was also a follow-up to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct maintenance window.\n   Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\", teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md\n\n2. #4419: Thea logged this one because the gatehouse barcode scanners weren't reading trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It went to tier-2 product support for firmware testing.\n   Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\", teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md\n\nTwo other Moss notes mention Quarrendon but give no ticket number: the 14 Sep 2025 pipeline digest and the 23 Mar 2026 renewal check-in. The Central handoffs digest has #4409, #4412 and FR-882, but those belong to Marrow accounts, not Quarrendon. Also, Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company that isn't a customer, so keep it out of the list.\n\nBefore this goes in the weekly notes:\n- I only checked Moss's notes that you have access to, so there may be more ticket numbers elsewhere.\n- The cheat sheet has no date, so check whether #4419 is still open."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DV03OPU0001","ts":"1791987000.000125"}}
